{"updated_at": {"date": {"d": "05", "m": "08", "Y": "2026"}, "time": {"H": "08", "M": "12", "S": "52"}}, "news": [{"title": "Gujarat: Draft rules bar PG facilities in new apartment blocks", "para": "Gujarat is set to revise its development control regulations by creating formal categories for PG facilities and preschools. The new rules prohibit the inclusion of PG accommodations in residential and commercial buildings, while preschools will fall under a designated 'Education-1' category with distinct construction requirements. This initiative aims to eliminate confusion and legal issues relating to these establishments. The state encourages public feedback until October 3.", "href": "https://realty.economictimes.indiatimes.com/news/residential/gujarat-draft-rules-bar-pg-facilities-in-new-apartment-blocks/132892373?utm_source=newslisting&utm_medium=latestNews", "img": "data:image/png;base64, ", "img-src": "https://etimg.etb2bimg.com/thumb/img-size-278060/132892373.cms?width=150&height=112", "tag": "residential"}, {"title": "Chandigarh's old housing societies seek relief from waste processing mandate", "para": "In Chandigarh, older housing societies face challenges adapting to new waste management regulations. With limited space for on-site processing facilities, residents advocate for a tailored compliance framework for their complexes. They express readiness to implement effective waste segregation and collection practices while requesting physical verification before any enforcement measures are enacted.", "href": "https://realty.economictimes.indiatimes.com/news/residential/chandigarhs-old-housing-societies-seek-relief-from-waste-processing-mandate/132892202?utm_source=newslisting&utm_medium=latestNews", "img": "data:image/png;base64, ", "img-src": "https://etimg.etb2bimg.com/thumb/img-size-310994/132892202.cms?width=150&height=112", "tag": "residential"}, {"title": "RBI keeps policy rate unchanged for third time in row amid West Asia crisis", "para": "The Reserve Bank of India maintained its key interest rates unchanged for the third consecutive time. This decision was made as the central bank considered global energy price uncertainties and supply disruptions. Inflation has now crossed the RBI's target, yet growth forecasts were slightly increased. The Indian rupee has experienced continuous depreciation against the US dollar this year. This currency decline is attributed to expensive oil and capital outflows.", "href": "https://realty.economictimes.indiatimes.com/news/industry/rbi-maintains-key-interest-rates-steady-amid-west-asia-turmoil/132893046?utm_source=newslisting&utm_medium=latestNews", "img": "data:image/png;base64, ", "img-src": "https://etimg.etb2bimg.com/thumb/img-size-69552/132893046.cms?width=150&height=112", "tag": "industry"}]}